 ### [Ray-Layer Buffer Generation via Depth Peeling](9474-ray-layer-buffer-generation-via-depth-peeling.md)
-Generates the ray-layer buffer by depth-peeling VOI definitions and grouping fragments into ordered layers based on VOI priority and material ID. It differs from standard GPU-based CSG by performing stencil-like tests inside a GPU program, preserving priority and ID information.
+Generates the ray-layer buffer by depth-peeling VOI definitions and grouping fragments into ordered layers based on VOI priority and material ID. It differs from standard GPU-based CSG by performing stencil-like tests inside a GPU program, preserving priority and ID information. Choose this method when rendering nested, potentially self-intersecting VOIs on the GPU where standard stencil buffers fail to preserve critical priority data.
 
 ### [Layer Separation Heuristic](11327-layer-separation-heuristic.md)
-Determines optimal split points along a ray to separate high-quality raycasting from lower-cost image warping. It identifies specific volumetric features for light attenuation, preserving depth cues better than simple depth-based splitting.
+Determines optimal split points along a ray to separate high-quality raycasting from lower-cost image warping. It identifies specific volumetric features for light attenuation, preserving depth cues better than simple depth-based splitting. Choose this method when rendering transparent volumes where the main visual effect occurs in the middle of a ray interval rather than at entry or exit.
 
